    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d947568b_4a8e1332",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-13T18:19:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does default to this. In other places in the code we set values when we rely on the value.  In this case these line up to the tcpc_vbus bits.",
      "parentUuid": "585fdde0_72fa7e93",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 111,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 111,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "db124d0f314bdaae7505f78481cc39e115e3e0a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "93303c11_fc6c1e9b",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-13T19:58:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we are relying on the values mapping to the tcpc_bus bits, then we should have a comment about it.\n\nHowever, I don\u0027t know that that we need to add that coupling as it doesn\u0027t really give us much especially with the vSrcValid value in this enum set",
      "parentUuid": "d947568b_4a8e1332",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 111,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 111,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "db124d0f314bdaae7505f78481cc39e115e3e0a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b6025da_4210c0c7",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-13T16:17:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what if we are at 20V? do we need another option?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "db124d0f314bdaae7505f78481cc39e115e3e0a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "702c87ec_59df3afe",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-13T18:19:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When we need it, we should add it.  I have not seen any code that looks for Safe20V",
      "parentUuid": "2b6025da_4210c0c7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "db124d0f314bdaae7505f78481cc39e115e3e0a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0fef0268_0f5e407c",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-13T19:09:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we\u0027ll need another mechanism for that. Eventually Type-C layer should be checking that VBUS is within vSrcValid. That could be anything with PPS and therefore, I don\u0027t think adding enum entries for those would be the way to go.",
      "parentUuid": "702c87ec_59df3afe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "db124d0f314bdaae7505f78481cc39e115e3e0a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
